Maintainer repair appended in 097b5dd and 1ed5c0d (no history rewrite).

Security corrections:
- rebased by merging current main (759bfd0) while preserving the newer orchestrator governance hook;
- explicit per-agent capability policies now take precedence over `_default`, so an agent-specific deny cannot inherit a wildcard grant;
- `shared` and `server` profiles fail closed if capability-policy or rate-limiter initialization fails;
- the primary served agent now receives the configured rate limiter;
- AuditLogger serializes the SQLite tail-read/hash/insert transaction and its other connection operations;
- added adversarial HTTP-server and managed-agent execution tests proving denied privileged tools never run, plus concurrent hash-chain coverage.

Validation:
- `ruff format` / `ruff check` on all touched files: pass
- focused server, managed-agent, setup-security and audit suites: 43 passed, 1 skipped
- fallback precedence branch exercised directly: pass

The one skipped local test requires the compiled `openjarvis_rust` extension. A local build could not link because this host has not accepted the Xcode license; hosted CI remains authoritative for the Rust-backed capability suite.

Appended second security repair commit `436e44b45533522b198e693e3b06fe16035cc600` after exact-head gating on `d7ffb2d5d97fd4c894b3ec9382845001188e3847` (non-force push).

This closes the remaining verifier bypasses:

- inventories canonical minimum capabilities for all 63 registered in-tree tools; only `calculator` and `think` are explicitly capability-free, and any future uninventoried built-in fails closed as `system:admin`;
- blocks real `repl`, Docker/code interpreters, user/profile/memory/skill management, browser interaction, knowledge aliases, scheduler, channel, proactive, and other privileged tools under default-deny unless their canonical capabilities are granted;
- preserves the selected runtime agent identity through both `SystemBuilder` skill executors, `jarvis ask`, `QueryOrchestrator`, server channels, scheduled execution, managed Deep Research SSE, and server-created messaging/webhook Deep Research agents;
- propagates configured rate limiting and audit/policy primitives through channel and scheduled `JarvisSystem` instances while avoiding unsupported security kwargs on `SimpleAgent`;
- makes `create_app(config=...)` derive missing security primitives fail-closed, create an audit-capable event bus, preserve explicit injections, and secure a pre-built tool agent/executor;
- serializes audit hash-chain tail-read plus append across logger instances/processes with SQLite `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` and a busy timeout.

Adversarial validation includes a real REPL with `_default` granted `code:execute` but the runtime caller explicitly denied, the same bypass through an executable nested skill, managed Deep Research capability denial plus runtime-specific rate keys, simple-agent serve startup, config-derived factory wiring, server channel/scheduler wiring, and four logger instances concurrently writing 400 events with a valid final hash chain.

Validation:

- `1442 passed, 7 skipped` — security + agents + serve/channel + full server matrices
- `372 passed` — MCP, learning executor, canonical tool-floor, security, managed-agent/server, and serve regression selection on final code
- focused repair gate: `103 passed`
- Ruff: all changed source/test files pass
- `compileall`: pass

The broader learning checkpoint/rollback selection also produced 947 passes; its nine failures were environment-only because macOS system `git` exits 69 until the Xcode license is accepted. No merge, close, draft, or review-state change was made.

Third security repair pushed append-only at 3c8c0c986289f9a76d17e39b43d5e8aa2bd7c8a2 (parent was exact live head 436e44b45533522b198e693e3b06fe16035cc600).

This closes the remaining verifier paths:
- centralized capability/rate/identity/audit-bus wiring for chat, SDK, ask, serve, system orchestration, managed executors, programmatic create_app, and lightweight managed-agent run/immediate facades;
- AgentSpawn/Kill/Send API operations now dispatch through the secured ToolExecutor;
- NativeOpenHands URL prefetch and RLM REPL execution now dispatch through canonical gates;
- direct execution gates for claude_code, opencode, openhands, mini_swe, hybrid SWE shells, and hybrid Tavily fetches;
- standalone Slack, iMessage, and deep-research launchers now derive and propagate configured security;
- MCP adapter provenance is resolved before tool names, with calculator/think safe floors pinned to the actual in-tree classes;
- ephemeral session flushes now use their requested memory/skill tools through a secured tool-capable agent;
- JarvisSystem rate_limiter moved after every pre-existing positional field.

Adversarial evidence:
- 400 focused/adjacent tests passed (security, agents, chat/serve/channel, SDK/system, API/app/managed routes).
- Clean broad run: 2179 passed, 9 skipped across tests/agents, tests/cli, tests/server, tests/sdk, tests/security, ToolExecutor and MCP adapter suites (excluding tests/cli/test_memory_cmd.py because this local compiled Rust extension is stale).
- The two excluded memory-index failures reproduce in isolation and are environment-only: builtins.SQLiteMemory lacks the current replace_source method.
- Full source Ruff, changed-test Ruff, compileall, and git diff --check passed.

No merge, close, draft, or review-state action was taken.

Maintainer repair pushed at `564d9ae` after reconciling the branch with current `main`.

What changed:
- centralized daemon and mining PID handling in the shared cross-platform utilities;
- retained the signal-free Windows `OpenProcess`/`WaitForSingleObject` liveness probe already established on `main`;
- made POSIX liveness treat unreaped zombies as exited (the old `kill(pid, 0)` loop could wait and escalate forever);
- kept graceful-then-forced termination semantics (`SIGTERM`/`SIGKILL` on POSIX, `taskkill` then `/F /T` on Windows);
- added simulated Windows coverage for missing, access-denied, exited, and live handles, plus graceful and forced `taskkill` command paths.

Verification:
- Ruff check and format check: clean.
- Focused process/daemon/mining tests: **49 passed**.
- Full `tests/core` + `tests/cli`: **736 passed, 2 skipped**. The two remaining memory-index failures reproduce unchanged on current `main` with this environment's stale Rust extension (`SQLiteMemory.replace_source` is absent), so they are not caused by this PR.
- The update passed an exact open-state/head-SHA/maintainer-modifiable gate and was pushed non-force to the contributor branch.
